From f593496f2d18b835fea51e3414efa6022e33aa58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:40:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Global Class / Mix leaderboards via the matchmaker; IB class
 rate tables

Card servers send salted, secret-free snapshots (name + stats only) to
/tag/leaderboard/submit with the shared /tag secret, every 10 min and
shortly after each saved Class / Mix result. The matchmaker stores rows
per server + opaque card key, ignores stale snapshots, rate/size/row
limits submissions, expires old rows, and serves /leaderboard (public
page + JSON, own per-IP limit, PublicPage switch). Card-server WebUI gets
a Leaderboards section (Class solo / Class team / Mix) and a "Show my
name" switch.

Class rate +0: LoadClassMatch only filled OverBoost fields, so IB cabinets
got initial_rate 0 and no grade thresholds. ClassRateTables (default on)
sends initial rate, grade bands and class-change rates;
ClassRateServerFallback (default off) applies a server-side delta when the
cabinet still reports +0.

deploy.sh keeps and backs up leaderboard state. Tests: Server.Tests +7,
Matchmaking.Tests +19.

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
