+## Global leaderboards (2026-11-16, branch `global-leaderboards`) — unit + local e2e tests, not yet on a VPS
+Three public boards per matchmaker region: **Class solo**, **Class team** and **Mix** (online free battles).
+Each card server sends a leaderboard snapshot of its own cards to the matchmaker; the matchmaker merges the
+snapshots and shows the boards.
+
+**Flow**
+* Card server → `POST {tag}/leaderboard/submit`. `{tag}` is the same `/tag` URL as online tag / friends, it needs
+  the same `X-Tag-Secret` header, and it uses the same `/tag` rate limit. A snapshot goes out 20 s after start,
+  every `SubmitIntervalMinutes` (10), and `SubmitAfterResultSeconds` (15) after each saved Class / Mix result.
+  It runs in the background and never delays a game reply.
+* A snapshot row holds:
+  * an opaque card key: HMAC-SHA256 of the local card id under a random salt (`leaderboard_salt.txt`) that stays on
+    that card server, first 16 bytes as hex;
+  * the card name, or no name when hidden;
+  * per-board wins, losses, class, grade, rate and top suit id.
+  
+  **It never contains an access code, chip id, boot token, local card id or the salt.**
+* Matchmaker: rows are stored per server id + card key in `leaderboard.json`. A full snapshot replaces that server's
+  rows. A snapshot no newer than the last one from that server, or older than `MaxSnapshotAgeHours`, is ignored
+  (`stale`). Other limits:
+
+  | Limit | Answer | Setting |
+  |---|---|---|
+  | Snapshot from the future | 400 | more than `MaxClockSkewMinutes` ahead |
+  | Snapshots per server | 429 | one per `MinSubmitIntervalSeconds` |
+  | Body size | 413 | `MaxSubmitBytes` |
+  | Rows | 400 | `MaxEntriesPerSubmit` |
+  | Rows per server / in total | extra rows rejected | `MaxEntriesPerServer` / `MaxTotalEntries` |
+  | Servers | 507 | `MaxServers` |
+
+  Rows a server has not refreshed for `EntryExpiryDays` are dropped. Names are cleaned like partner-code names (max
+  32 characters), and numbers are clamped.
+* Public read:
+  * `GET /leaderboard` is a small HTML page with tabs; it shows `RegionName`.
+  * `GET /leaderboard/data?board=class-solo|class-team|mix&limit=` returns JSON with rank, name (null when
+    hidden), class, grade, rate, wins, losses, matches, win rate and top suit id. It has no keys and no server ids.
+  * In `PublicMatchmaker` mode the internet may reach `/leaderboard` only when `Leaderboard.Enabled` and
+    `PublicPage` are both on. It has its own per-IP limit (`PublicRequestsPerMinute` / `PublicBurst`).
+  * Card servers read the boards via `GET {tag}/leaderboard/{board}` (with the secret).
+* Card-server WebUI:
+  * The front page has a **Leaderboards** section (also `/GlobalLeaderboards` and the nav menu) with Class solo /
+    Class team / Mix tabs, suit pictures and names. It is cached for `ViewCacheSeconds`.
+  * View Card → Stats has a **Show my name on the global leaderboards** switch, which saves to
+    `leaderboard_hidden.json`. The switch sends the access code and chip id in a POST body only, and the server
+    logs only the card id.
+* Ordering:
+  * Class boards: class, then rate, then the Wilson 95% lower bound of the win rate, then matches.
+  * Mix: Wilson lower bound, then wins, then matches. A 5-0 card does not outrank a 45-5 card.
+  * Only cards with at least `MinMatches` (5) matches on that board are ranked.
+* All-in-one server (no separate matchmaker): the in-process store is used, with the same rules.
+
+**Settings** (`CardServerConfig.Leaderboard`; every value has a default, so an old `server.json` works unchanged)
+
+| Side | Setting | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| both | `Enabled` | true | master switch (off: no submit, no boards, `/leaderboard` 404) |
+| card | `SubmitEnabled` | true | send snapshots |
+| card | `SubmitIntervalMinutes` / `SubmitAfterResultSeconds` | 10 / 15 | periodic / after-result snapshot |
+| card | `SubmitMinMatches` | 1 | only cards with this many board matches are sent |
+| card | `HideNamesByDefault` | false | true = names hidden until the player turns "Show my name" on |
+| card | `SaltFile` / `HiddenFile` | `leaderboard_salt.txt` / `leaderboard_hidden.json` | private salt / name opt-outs |
+| card | `ViewCacheSeconds` | 30 | WebUI board cache |
+| matchmaker | `AcceptSubmissions` | true | accept `/tag/leaderboard/submit` (off: 404) |
+| matchmaker | `RegionName` | "" | label on the boards (e.g. "LA", "EU") |
+| matchmaker | `MinMatches` / `MaxRows` | 5 / 100 | ranking threshold / rows per board |
+| matchmaker | `PublicPage` | true | serve `/leaderboard` (internet in PublicMatchmaker mode) |
+| matchmaker | `PublicRequestsPerMinute` / `PublicBurst` | 60 / 20 | per-IP limit for `/leaderboard` |
+| matchmaker | `MinSubmitIntervalSeconds`, `MaxSubmitBytes`, `MaxEntriesPerSubmit`, `MaxEntriesPerServer`, `MaxTotalEntries`, `MaxServers`, `EntryExpiryDays`, `MaxClockSkewMinutes`, `MaxSnapshotAgeHours`, `StateFile` | 20, 512 KiB, 2000, 5000, 100000, 1000, 60, 10, 24, `leaderboard.json` | abuse limits / storage |
+
+**Class rate stuck at 1500 (+0)**
+
+*Finding.* Every Class result on 14 and 16 November reported `before=after=1500, obtained 0, grade 0`, for winners
+and losers, solo and team. The cabinet computes the rate itself, and the server only stores it. The cause:
+upstream's `LoadClassMatch` reply fills only OverBoost-era fields (`ProtoIgnore` on IB). An IB cabinet therefore got
+`initial_rate` 0, no grade thresholds and no class-change rates.
+
+*Fix* (`OnlineMatching.ClassRateTables`, default on):
+
+* The reply now carries `initial_rate` = `ClassInitialRate` (1500).
+* It carries grade thresholds for solo classes 1–4 and team classes 2–4: 10 contiguous bands of
+  `ClassGradeRateStep` (100), with 1500 in grade 5.
+* It carries class-change initial rates.
+
+*Fallback* (`OnlineMatching.ClassRateServerFallback`, default **off**): if the cabinet still reports +0, the server
+applies upstream's documented formula: a win gives `+10 × (1 + score / 25000)` and a loss gives `−10`. The log line
+then ends with `server-fallback ±x`.
+
+Both are untested on a cabinet. The cabinet's own formula has not been reverse engineered.
+
+**Tests**
+* `Tests/Server.Tests/LeaderboardTests.cs` (7): snapshot contents and no secrets, min matches, hidden / opt-in,
+  identity persistence, result → snapshot → board, class tables on the wire, tables off, fallback.
+* `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/LeaderboardStoreTests.cs` (19): ordering, Wilson, min matches, stale / old / future,
+  bad input, bad / duplicate keys, full-snapshot removal, interval 429, caps / 507, hidden names, clamping,
+  persistence and expiry, off = 404, board names, public path rule.
+* `server-sketch/loadtest/leaderboard_e2e.py` (exvs2-lobbies repo, 44 checks): two servers, results on B → boards
+  on A, HTML page, secret required, 413 / stale / 400s, WebUI proxy, hide / show name, and no access code / chip id /
+  salt / key in A's public output, files or logs.
+
 ## Known gaps / risks
 * CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
   (`BindMatchNodesToSourceIp` limits Check/Cancel to the IP that entered, but is not a login.)
