 - `/tag` needs the shared secret (`OnlineTag.TagSecret`, header `X-Tag-Secret`). It lives only in the VPS
   `Configurations/server.json` (0640 root:exvs2mm) and in each card server's `server.json`. Set or rotate it with
   `deploy.sh --tag-secret-file FILE`, then put the same value in every card server and restart them.
-- `deploy.sh` never deletes `tag_invites.json`, `friends.json` and `tag_server_id.txt`, and copies
+- `deploy.sh` never deletes `tag_invites.json`, `friends.json`, `leaderboard*.json` and `tag_server_id.txt`, and copies
   `tag_invites.json` / `friends.json` to `<name>.bak-<UTC timestamp>` before each upload.
 - Friends (2026-11-15) use `/tag/friends/...` on the same port, secret and rate limit as `/tag`; no firewall or
   config change is needed. `CardServerConfig.Friends` defaults are fine (Enabled, AutoCreateTagTeam, SendNgList).
+- Global leaderboards (2026-11-16):
+  - Card servers send snapshots to `/tag/leaderboard/submit`, on the same port, secret and limits as `/tag`.
+  - The internet may also read `http://<VPS_IP>:28090/leaderboard`, a public page plus `/leaderboard/data` JSON
+    with names and stats only. It has its own per-IP limit, and `Leaderboard.PublicPage=false` turns it off.
+  - Set `CardServerConfig.Leaderboard.RegionName` (e.g. `"LA"` / `"EU"`) in the VPS `server.json`. Without it the
+    defaults apply: `MinMatches` 5, `MaxRows` 100, submissions on.
+  - State is kept in `leaderboard.json`. `deploy.sh` keeps it and backs it up before each upload.
 
 ## Pointing a local card server at it
 In that card server's `Configurations/server.json` -> `CardServerConfig.OnlineMatching`:
